        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Kalooki (Caribbean)',
            subtitle: 'The Caribbean Classic',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Kalooki (specifically the Caribbean or Jamaican version) is a high-stakes, 108-card contract rummy game. Played over nine rounds with increasing difficulty, it requires players to complete specific 'contracts' of sets (threes) and runs (fours). It is a central part of Caribbean social life and is known for the 'Call' mechanic where players can snatch discards out of turn.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Derived from European Rummy games (like Kalooki 40), it was heavily adapted in Jamaica to include the 'out-of-turn call' and specific contract escalations.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard with 4-5 players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two standard decks and four Jokers (Total 108 cards).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '108 cards, score sheet, chips for stakes (optional)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Varies by round: Hand 1 (9 cards), Hand 2 (10), ... Hand 9 (16 cards).',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Super Kalooki: High-stakes version played starting from Hand 5.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Baby Kalooki: Shorter 5-round version.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'European Kalooki: Different contract requirements and Joker rules.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
    description: "Kalooki (specifically the Caribbean or Jamaican version) is a high-stakes, 108-card contract rummy game. Played over nine rounds with increasing difficulty, it requires players to complete specific 'contracts' of sets (threes) and runs (fours). It is a central part of Caribbean social life and is known for the 'Call' mechanic where players can snatch discards out of turn.",
